  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to KP-4 through a shared intermediate molecule, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which acts as a target for multiple drug entities. This molecule is identified as a target of doxorubicin, NCI-H46, and NCI-H1304, all of which are distinct cell lines. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin exerts its biological effect via a pathway that involves the activation of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets KP-4. The consistent presence of this intermediate across different targets implies a mechanistic link between doxorubicin and KP-4, likely through a common biochemical pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a bridge between doxorubicin and KP-4, underscoring the importance of this molecule in the drug's action.",
